<section class="submit">
    <div class="submit-card">
        <p class="submit-kicker">FINISHED YOUR PROJECT?</p>
        <h2>Measure your ship.<br />Submit it.</h2>
        <ol class="steps">
            <li><span>01</span>Build</li>
            <li><span>02</span>Measure</li>
            <li><span>03</span>Submit</li>
        </ol>
        <a class="button button-dark" href="https://forms.hackclub.com/mini-submission">Submit your project <span>↗</span></a>
        <p class="eligibility">Open worldwide to teens ages 13 to 18. No experience required.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="mini-faq">
        <details>
            <summary>Who is eligible?</summary>
            <p>Teens ages 13 to 18 (inclusive), in high school, from any country and at any skill level.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
            <summary>I'm stuck! Where do I get help?</summary>
            <p>Join the <a href="https://hackclub.com/slack">Hack Club Slack</a>, and ask for help in the <a href="https://hackclub.enterprise.slack.com/archives/C0BPMT54UDD">#mini-ysws</a> channel!</p>
        </details>
        <details>
            <summary>What is Hack Club?</summary>
            <p>
                Hack Club is a 501(c)3 non-profit organization (really, it's the people), and we've run a bunch of events like this in the past. For example, we ran a 180-person hardware hackathon at GitHub HQ, and a seven-day game jam in Shanghai, China.
            </p>
        </details>
        <details>
            <summary>Can I submit to this event and another Hack Club program?</summary>
            Sorry, nope! "Double-dipping" is not allowed. If you make a project for this event, you can only submit it here, unless another program specifically states otherwise.
        </details>
        <details>
            <summary>How do I measure my website?</summary>
            You can use either Cloudflare Radar, or the network tab inside your browser's Devtools. You'll be looking for "Data Transferred".
        </details>
    </div>
</section>

<footer class="home-footer">
    <a class="mini-mark" href="#top" aria-label="Back to top"><span>mini</span></a>
    <p>A small project by <a href="https://hackclub.com">Hack Club</a>. A program by @hna </p>
    <a href="#top">Back to top ↑</a>
</footer>
